cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use blind-counsel or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "blind-counsel: confidential legal AI on a zero-trust cloud without TEEs"
abstract: >-
  A research proof of concept. It shows that hiding client data inside an open-weight LLM
  run by an untrusted cloud (a keyed, function-preserving weight shift) fails: the
  operator recovers 100% of the secret content from public-vs-deployed weight statistics,
  through fine-tuning. It then demonstrates a working alternative: public-law reasoning
  precomputed in the cloud and fetched with private information retrieval (PIR), applied
  to the confidential client account on the lawyer's own laptop, with code doing the
  arithmetic. No client data reaches the cloud, and the cloud cannot tell which matter it
  served.
